WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.534
-Our first guest tonight
is a talented actor and comedian

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:04.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know from his work
as Ali G., Bruno, and Borat.

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:08.108
He wrote, produced, and starre
in "Borat Subsequent Moviefilm,"

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:10.176 size:78% position:39%
for which he received
an Oscar nomination

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
and WGA award for
Best Adapted Screenplay.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:16.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
He is also nominated for a
Oscar for Best Supporting Acto

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
for his performance
as Abbie Hoffman

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:20.420 line:92%
in "The Trial of the Chicago 7."

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.221 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:24.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know why
you're on trial here?

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:28.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We carried certain ideas
across state lines.

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:32.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not machine guns
or drugs or little girls.

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:33.366 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Ideas.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:36.269
When we crossed from New Yor
to New Jersey to Pennsylvani

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:40.507 size:78% position:39%
to Ohio to Illinois,
we had certain ideas.

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:43.576 line:92%
And for that, we were gassed

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
beaten, arrested,
and put on trial.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:48.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome to the sho
Sacha Baron Cohen.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:50.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are you, Sacha?
-Hi, good.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:52.886 size:81% position:41%
How's it going, Seth?
-It's going very well.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.989 size:81% position:41%
It's incredible to me
not only how wonderful

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.957
both these performances are,
but the fact that you were

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
doing them simultaneously
is shocking to me

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:03.096
because it's -- obviously,
they're two very different sets.

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:08.234
One is very controlled, an
then, of course, you have Borat.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:12.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. I mean,
on the set of "Chicago 7,"

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.374 line:92%
you can go to craft services

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:16.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know,
you can go to a trailer.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:19.079 size:81% position:41% line:92%
On the set of "Borat,"

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:21.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're basically running awa
from the police.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you meet in between.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:26.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, it's so funny,
because, of course, that's wha

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:28.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
Abbie Hoffman
goes through in real life.

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:31.691
And it's what you put yourself
through as an actor as Borat

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:34.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, Abbie Hoffman
was someone who used clownin

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:36.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
to sort of
make political points.

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:39.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
Very different from Borat,
obviously,

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.267 line:92%
in what they were aiming to do

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
but there
are some similarities there.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:47.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I mean --
I almost found Abbie

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:49.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
this really
inspirational character.

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:52.679 size:88% position:44%
I first read about him
when I was in university

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:53.446 size:75% position:38% line:92%
when I was about 20.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:59.119
And he was really hilarious,
brilliantly clever, and --

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:01.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
but fundamentally,
like, this really brave,

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:05.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
courageous activist who,
you know, actually was ready

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:09.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
to die to fight injustice,
which is not a very funny thin

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:12.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
to say on a late-night show,
but I've done it.

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:15.034
-Well, it's interesting, though,
because I do feel like

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:21.241
this "Borat" was certainly mor
political than the last one.

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:23.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
And in a way,
you were putting yourself

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.812 line:92%
in fairly dangerous situations

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:29.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
You must realize, like,
there is some parallel now

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
to what Abbie Hoffman
was doing a long time ago.

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:35.889
-Well, I never really wanted
to do another Borat movie,

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:37.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then,
Donald Trump came along,

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:42.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I got increasingly angry
with some of the things

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:45.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
that were going on --
the Muslim ban, et cetera.

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, it's coming up
to the election,

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:51.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I felt I needed to put
the gray suit on again just to

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:57.343
you know, put out somethin
to show that I didn't agree.

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.979
And we really just wanted it
to come out before the election.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:05.385
So the whole crew put themselves
through crazy experiences

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:06.853 line:92%
and put themselves at real risk.

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, you know, obviously,
you have just

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:11.991
the logistical challenges
of something like CPAC,

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:13.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I want to ask about
in a minute,

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:15.962
and then you have the challenges
of writing a script.

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:18.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, of course,
the core of Borat

00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:21.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
is this performance
and this character you become.

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:24.938 line:92%
And you went to clowning school.

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:26.739 line:92%
Was that actually in France?

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:31.711
-That was a French teacher
called Philippe Gaulier.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:34.047 line:92%
And luckily, it was in London.

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:35.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
People would fly
from around the world.

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:40.253
There were people from Australia
flown to -- to study with him.

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:41.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, basically,
the first thing you would do

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:44.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
is you put some clown music,
you put on your red nose,

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:45.592 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
go around the room.

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:50.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
If he hit his drum,
you would have to sit down

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.097 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And that was it.

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:52.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was the end
of your exercise.

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:55.368
And you'd have people who'
flown in from Australia,

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:57.737 size:81% position:41%
the clown music goes,
stops the clown music,

00:03:57.737 --> 00:04:00.940 size:78% position:39%
they start speaking,
and he hits his drum,

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:01.641 line:92%
'cause they're not funny.

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:05.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they would burst into tear
and hate him.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Very sad.
Just sad to think of anyon

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:09.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
crying in their
full clown costume.

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:12.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly. Exactly.
Sad clown.

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:16.923
-Is this a -- is this a clow
teacher who is proud of the work

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:18.491 line:92%
that you have done in the year

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:20.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
since you were under
his tutelage?

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:22.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I'm still
in contact with him,

00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:24.530
and I'll call him up,
and I'll go, "What do you think?

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
How was that?"
and he'll often go,

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:28.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
"That was [bleep]"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:32.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
"It was not good.
You are not funny.

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:36.376
We did not like this character."
You know, so...

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:39.612
Yeah, it keeps -- he's very good
at keeping me down.

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:43.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is it true that,
even before Ali G.,

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:46.085 line:92%
you worked on a kids show?

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:48.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was a --
I was bizarrely,

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:53.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
given my lack of personality
the host of a show.

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:54.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
Admittedly,
it was for teenagers,

00:04:54.661 --> 00:05:01.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I wanted to get out
of the job and be a comedian

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:02.935 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But it was --

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:06.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't know anyone in London
who had that job.

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:07.173 line:92%
I didn't even know any actors.

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:11.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I basically started
doing these little character

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:14.047 size:75% position:38% line:92%
live on the TV show.

00:05:14.047 --> 00:05:16.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I would go out
and shoot beforehand.

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:20.486
And the idea was they'd play i
and react to what was going on

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:25.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one of the characters
actually was Borat.

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:27.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, first time I ever
took him out

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:32.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
was at a fox-hunting rally
in London

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:33.733 line:92%
outside the House of Parliament.

00:05:33.733 --> 00:05:36.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a bunch of members
of the upper class going out

00:05:36.102 --> 00:05:38.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
to say that
they should keep fox hunting

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:41.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it's an important
English tradition.

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:47.347
And I went out and basically
pretended to be from Moldova

00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:50.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was, "Hello.
I'm from Moldova telebisk.

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:52.819 line:92%
In my country, we hunt Jews.

00:05:52.819 --> 00:05:57.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
We give them a head start,
and then we hunt them.

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:58.925 line:92%
You think we should do it here?"

00:05:58.925 --> 00:06:02.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they'd say,
"Well, I suppose if it was -

00:06:02.462 --> 00:06:07.233
if it was a fair start, at least
20 or 30 minutes, then yes."

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:11.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, yeah, so that was
the birth of Ali G. and Borat,

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:13.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
and eventually,
I left that kids show.

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:15.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, everyone
at the kids show hated it.

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:19.679
By the way, when I put those -
when I actually put those things

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:22.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the TV show,
I immediately got brought in

00:06:22.382 --> 00:06:23.383 size:88% position:44% line:92%
to the head of the show,

00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:26.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he said, "Do that agai
and you are fired."

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:28.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, in fact,
they not only fired me,

00:06:28.721 --> 00:06:30.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
they shut down
the entire channel.

00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:32.725 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:34.627 line:92%
-Well, that's a nice legacy.

